"ASM-205" [label="ASM-205: It is assumed that the hardware\nplatform (STM32U5) possesses a functional\nand configurable Memory Protection\nUnit (MPU) or TrustZone capability.\n", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"ASM-207" [label="ASM-207: It is assumed that the vehicle\npossesses a secondary source for\nspeed estimation (e.g., IMU or motor\nmodel) with a known error margin.\n", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"ASM-300" [label="ASM-300: All tasks accessing shared\nspeed data use the designated RTOS\nsynchronization   primitives and\ndo not bypass them through direct\nor unsafe memory access. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"ASM-301" [label="ASM-301: The RTOS is correctly configured\nand supports priority inheritance\nor an   equivalent mechanism for\nmanaging priority inversion. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"ASM-400" [label="ASM-400: It is assumed that both\nends of the communication (RPi and\nSTM32) use the same version of the\nVSS specification file (.vspec) to\navoid mapping conflicts. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"ASM-501" [label="ASM-501: Communication latency remains\nwithin the limits defined by the\nsystem architecture. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"ASM-504" [label="ASM-504: The instrument cluster hardware\nis powered continuously since the\nstart of the vehicle operation. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
