"AST-201" [label="AST-201: If the time counter between\npulses exceeds the calibrated threshold\n(e.g., 500ms), the system MUST transition\nto the \"Signal Lost\" error state.\n", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-202" [label="AST-202: Pulses with a width smaller\nthan the configured debouncing minimum\ntime MUST be ignored by the speed\ncounter. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-205" [label="AST-205: The firmware MUST configure\nthe Memory Protection Unit (MPU)\nto enforce read-only access to the\nsensor driver code and restricted\nread/write access to its data structures,\ntriggering a fault on unauthorized\naccess. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-206" [label="AST-206: If the capture timer overflows,\nthe calculation logic MUST handle\nthe event to prevent the speed from\nbeing calculated as zero or an incorrect\nmomentary value. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-207" [label="AST-207: The system MUST compare\nthe calculated wheel speed against\na secondary estimation source (e.g.,\nIMU) and invalidate the reading if\nthe deviation exceeds the defined\nerror margin. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-300" [label="AST-300: The speed sensor task executes\nperiodically within its configured\nperiod and   completes execution\nbefore its defined deadline on every\nactivation under   normal operating\nconditions. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-301" [label="AST-301: Every speed sample produced\nby the system includes a monotonic\ntimestamp, and   samples older than\nthe configured freshness threshold\nare automatically   invalidated and\nnot used by downstream control logic.\n", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-302" [label="AST-302: Concurrent tasks accessing\nshared speed data are synchronized\nusing RTOS   primitives such that\nno data races, partial writes, or\ninconsistent reads   occur during\nexecution. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-303" [label="AST-303: The system detects queue\noverflows and lost messages in inter-task\n  communication and reports these\nevents through logs or diagnostic\ncounters   at runtime. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-304" [label="AST-304: The RTOS configuration prevents\nunbounded priority inversion by ensuring\nthat   safety-critical tasks are\nprotected by priority inheritance\nor equivalent   mechanisms, maintaining\nbounded execution latency. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-400" [label="AST-400: Not only should the variables\nbe conventionally aligned with the\nVSS standard, but the units of measurement\nshould also be. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-401" [label="AST-401: The code must have a data\nrange validator, if the information\nsent has a value beyond the max,\nor less than the min of the range\nit must be discarded. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-501" [label="AST-501: The instrument cluster shall\nrefresh each displayed vehicle parameter\nat least once every 300 ms. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-502" [label="AST-502: The instrument cluster shall\ndetect and flag any vehicle parameter\nthat is not updated within the defined\nfreshness time limit (300ms). ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-503" [label="AST-503: The instrument cluster shall\nnot crash, freeze, or display undefined\nbehavior when receiving invalid,\nmissing, or out-of-range vehicle\ndata. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-504" [label="AST-504: The instrument cluster shall\ndisplay a visible warning indication\nwhenever a critical vehicle condition\nis reported by the system. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-600" [label="AST-600: The system shall immediately\nstart Instrument Cluster using systemd\nmaximum 10 seconds after boot. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-601" [label="AST-601: The system shall immediately\nstart a script to verify OTA updates\nafter connected to the internet ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-602" [label="AST-602: If for any reason the auto-start\nof an application fails, the system\nshould attempt to run it again at\nleast 10 more times. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-603" [label="AST-603: The AGL on the Raspberry\nPi 5 must support the entire structure\nof this project and its features.\n", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-604" [label="AST-604: The system must include\na storage monitoring program. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-605" [label="AST-605: The system must include\na temperature monitoring program.\n", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-700" [label="AST-700: The new cluster version\nshall only start on the next time\nthe vehicle turn on again ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-701" [label="AST-701: The new package shall be\nvalidated using checksum or hash\nbefore installation ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-702" [label="AST-702: If the update fail (wifi,\nenergy drops etc...) the system shall\nsupport rollback to the previous\nversions. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-703" [label="AST-703: If the new package update\nis not safe the system shall support\nrollback to the previous versions.\n", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"AST-704" [label="AST-704: Every OTA update shall be\nlogged with timestamp, version and\nresult (success or fail) ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
