"EVD-ASM-205" [label="EVD-ASM-205: Technical evidence based\non the STM32U5 datasheet, confirming\nthe presence and capabilities of\nthe Memory Protection Unit (MPU).\n", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EVD-ASM-207" [label="EVD-ASM-207: Verification of vehicle\nspecifications, confirming that the\nIMU hardware is available and functional\nfor secondary speed estimation. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-100" [label="EXP-100: The CAN bus shall operate\nat 500 kbps with a bus load of less\nthan 70%. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-101" [label="EXP-101: The dynamic control messages\n(SPEED, MOTOR_PWR, STEER) shall be\ntransmitted cyclically every 50ms\n±10%. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-102" [label="EXP-102: Monitoring messages (BATTERY,\nTEMPERATURE) should be transmitted\nevery 1000ms ±10%. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-103" [label="EXP-103: The Emergency command (ESTOP\n- ID 0x001) must be processed and\nactivated on the STM32 in less than\n20ms from the request on the Rasp5.\n", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-201" [label="EXP-201: The speed sensor pulse reading\nlogic MUST be reliable and detect\ntimeouts (missing pulses) within\na safety-critical window to prevent\nstale data usage. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-202" [label="EXP-202: The software shall apply\nfiltering mechanisms (such as debouncing)\nto reject spurious pulses and ensure\nthat only valid signals are counted.\n", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-205" [label="EXP-205: The sensor driver interrupt\nand processing logic shall execute\nin an isolated memory region (MPU\nor TrustZone) to prevent external\ninterference. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-206" [label="EXP-206: The speed calculation algorithm\nshall correctly handle hardware counter\noverflow to maintain speed accuracy.\n", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-207" [label="EXP-207: The system shall cross-reference\nspeedometer data with a secondary\nspeed estimate (such as IMU derivative)\nto identify inconsistencies. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-300" [label="EXP-300: The system shall guarantee\nthat the task responsible for reading\nthe speed   sensor is executed periodically\nwithin its defined deadline, ensuring\ntemporal   predictability in the\nThreadX environment and preventing\ndelays that could   compromise vehicle\ncontrol. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-301" [label="EXP-301: The system shall ensure\nthat every speed sample includes\nan associated   monotonic timestamp\nand that stale data is automatically\ninvalidated when it   exceeds the\nmaximum allowed age, preventing the\nuse of outdated information   in\nvehicle control. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-302" [label="EXP-302: The system shall guarantee\nexclusive and deterministic access\nto speed data   shared between concurrent\ntasks, using RTOS synchronization\nprimitives to   prevent race conditions\nand data corruption. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-303" [label="EXP-303: The system shall detect\nand report queue overflows and lost\nmessages in   inter-task communication,\nensuring visibility of communication\nfailures that   could compromise\nthe integrity of speed data. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-304" [label="EXP-304: The system shall prevent\nunbounded priority inversion in safety-critical\n  tasks by ensuring that RTOS priority\ninheritance mechanisms are correctly\n  used to maintain predictable latency\nin the execution of speed-related\n  tasks. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-400" [label="EXP-400: All software components\nshall perform data transmission with\nunit conversion according to the\nVSS standard. Example: speed should\nbe treated as m/s. H1-400 ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-401" [label="EXP-401: The control system shall\nconsult VSS metadata (min/max) for\neach actuator signal. Commands that\nexceed these limits must trigger\nan integrity error. H2-400 ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-501" [label="EXP-501: The instrument cluster shall\nensure that displayed vehicle information\nrepresents the current system state\nwithin an acceptable time window\nand shall safely handle invalid,\nmissing, or out-of-range data without\ncausing application failure or undefined\nbehavior. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-502" [label="EXP-502: The instrument cluster shall\npresent warning and status indications\nwhenever critical vehicle conditions\nare detected, ensuring observer awareness.\n", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-600" [label="EXP-600: The system must automatically\nlaunch all applications necessary\nfor the project to function properly\nduring boot. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-601" [label="EXP-601: The system (AGL on Raspberry\nPi) has conditions to store all the\ndata necessary for its operation\nwithout risk of failure due to lack\nof space. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-602" [label="EXP-602: The AGL system on Raspberry\nPi continuously monitors key parameters\nsuch as temperature and voltage to\nprevent abrupt shutdowns and protect\nthe file system from corruption.\n", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-700" [label="EXP-700: The instrument cluster shall\nbe be updated at appropriate times\nand in a security way, ensuring the\nintegrity of the data displayed in\nthe vehicle. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
"EXP-701" [label="EXP-701: All over-the-air (OTA) updates\nare performed securely, ensuring\ndata integrity and preventing any\ncorruption or tampering that could\naffect system functionality. ", URL="", target="_top", shape=box, fontname="Open Sans"];
